WEBVTT

01:04.790 --> 01:05.920
Jasmine...

01:09.570 --> 01:10.670
Jasmine!

01:16.020 --> 01:16.970
I guess I lose.

01:16.970 --> 01:18.970
And that's our fault?!

02:49.320 --> 02:55.530
#3 The King Is Stranded.

02:50.060 --> 02:51.920
Let's go over the situation.

02:52.240 --> 02:56.540
I had taken a commission to capture a 
mana beast from the Helstea family.

02:57.060 --> 02:59.780
Until I was caught in a storm...

02:59.780 --> 03:02.040
I was on a job from the guild.

03:02.040 --> 03:03.840
There's been a series of 
fishing boats being lost

03:03.840 --> 03:05.290
in the waters near some farmland,

03:05.290 --> 03:09.960
and I was supposed to investigate the 
cause... when I was caught in a storm.

03:11.050 --> 03:13.410
You two are pathetic.

03:13.410 --> 03:17.060
It's hard to believe you're 
A-rank adventurers, like me.

03:20.090 --> 03:22.060
<i>The same thing happened to you!</i>

03:24.290 --> 03:26.710
This is the boat that 
Jasmine and I were in.

03:26.710 --> 03:28.060
I see.

03:28.060 --> 03:29.710
Hopefully she's all right.

03:31.440 --> 03:36.620
Well, it's in no shape to be of any use!
Now what're we supposed to do?

03:36.620 --> 03:38.330
Lucas, are you seriously—

03:38.330 --> 03:39.880
It's fine, Elijah.

03:39.880 --> 03:41.070
But...

03:41.500 --> 03:46.580
We need a boat.
 Lucas has a point about that.

03:47.010 --> 03:48.120
Obviously!

03:48.120 --> 03:50.960
You can be pretty mature, Note.

03:54.900 --> 03:59.830
<i>If I survived, I have 
no doubts that she did.</i>

04:09.260 --> 04:11.010
<i>Sylvie, can you hear me?</i>

04:11.010 --> 04:13.730
<i>I can. What's up, Papa?</i>

04:13.730 --> 04:18.160
<i>I'm in a bit of trouble. Could you 
do me a favor and find Jasmine?</i>

04:18.160 --> 04:20.900
<i>Sure. Where should I look?</i>

04:20.900 --> 04:22.160
<i>By the sea.</i>

04:22.160 --> 04:23.490
<i>You'll wanna look...</i>

04:25.970 --> 04:29.830
Note! If you can hear me, answer! Note?

04:35.740 --> 04:37.040
This is my fault.

04:38.540 --> 04:43.280
Regarding the arachne... frankly, 
there's still a lot we don't know.

04:43.600 --> 04:47.060
But there have apparently been 
other, similar cases happening.

04:47.570 --> 04:49.060
There's even more?

04:50.880 --> 04:55.530
A group goes out on a C-ranked job, 
but encounters an A-rank mana beast.

04:55.530 --> 04:58.320
There's been no shortage 
of stories like that.

04:58.780 --> 05:00.540
Could the guild be 
misjudging the jobs?

05:00.540 --> 05:02.400
It's not out of the question.

05:02.400 --> 05:05.830
The three-kingdom treaty has made 
things confusing for the guild, too.

05:06.130 --> 05:08.300
But there's a chance that someone

05:08.300 --> 05:11.080
opposed to the treaty is 
causing these accidents.

05:11.360 --> 05:12.920
Not that I have any proof.

05:14.780 --> 05:18.940
As his father, I would honestly rather 
he stop adventuring because of this.

05:18.940 --> 05:20.820
I don't think Arthur intends to stop.

05:21.580 --> 05:24.600
Well, he gets his stubbornness from Alice.

05:26.850 --> 05:31.550
As things stand, the best 
we can do is stay on our toes.

05:31.550 --> 05:35.320
When you head out on a quest, 
be more cautious than ever before.

05:37.260 --> 05:40.100
Jasmine, look after my boy.

05:42.000 --> 05:43.080
I know.

05:48.380 --> 05:49.370
Note!

05:49.370 --> 05:51.480
Master Lucas!

05:51.480 --> 05:53.120
Please, respond!

05:53.960 --> 05:56.040
So much for my luck.

05:57.410 --> 05:59.930
Then you two work for the Wykes.

05:59.930 --> 06:04.980
Yes. We were sent here by 
the Sapin royal family...

06:04.980 --> 06:07.420
but a storm hit, and we found
 ourselves here without...

06:08.900 --> 06:11.140
...the young master!

06:11.140 --> 06:12.440
A storm...

06:11.140 --> 06:14.020
Oh, Master, please be all right!

06:14.020 --> 06:16.650
Master Lucas!

06:16.650 --> 06:19.150
Young Master!

06:24.440 --> 06:26.270
A dimensional ring.

06:26.270 --> 06:28.660
<i>I've never seen one in person.</i>

06:28.660 --> 06:30.930
<i>I'd considered getting one myself before,</i>

06:30.930 --> 06:34.600
<i>but even at the lowest rank, 
they cost several thousand gold.</i>

06:35.280 --> 06:36.620
You don't have one?

06:37.010 --> 06:38.420
Sadly, no.

06:40.840 --> 06:42.340
You two can take care of it from here.

06:45.330 --> 06:47.850
What? You don't even know 
how to set up a tent?

06:47.850 --> 06:49.930
I could ask the same of you!

06:49.930 --> 06:51.440
Easy, there.

06:53.930 --> 06:55.940
You know your stuff.

06:55.940 --> 06:57.830
My partner taught me how.

06:57.830 --> 06:59.730
Hey, I'm hungry.

06:59.730 --> 07:02.190
Is there no food inside your ring?

07:05.720 --> 07:07.970
I'll take that as a no.

07:07.970 --> 07:11.620
He probably had his 
underlings collect food.

07:11.620 --> 07:12.520
Do you have anything?

07:12.520 --> 07:15.290
A bit, but with three of us,
 it'd be gone in one day.

07:15.290 --> 07:17.460
I see. In that case...

07:20.800 --> 07:22.380
This should cover us, right?

07:22.380 --> 07:26.060
Amazing! You can do just 
about anything, can't you?

07:28.410 --> 07:30.500
Handle the fish, Lucas.

07:31.360 --> 07:33.080
Do a good job cooking them.

07:34.640 --> 07:36.060
Why should I?!

07:36.060 --> 07:39.330
You're the one here who's most 
skilled with fire magic, right?

07:39.330 --> 07:40.480
Obviously.

07:40.820 --> 07:42.230
So, it's up to you.

07:44.620 --> 07:47.240
I guess I'll have to.

07:53.250 --> 07:55.650
Try to leave enough 
for us to actually eat.

07:55.650 --> 07:57.250
I know!

08:00.660 --> 08:01.880
Make sure it's actually cooked.

08:01.880 --> 08:03.500
I get it, all right?!

08:11.930 --> 08:16.020
Look at that! Expect 
nothing less from a Wykes!

08:18.620 --> 08:20.990
They'll be good to eat once 
the juices start to surface.

08:21.320 --> 08:22.750
You really do know your stuff!

08:22.750 --> 08:24.530
Pay attention!

08:31.210 --> 08:32.530
Not bad at all.

08:32.980 --> 08:36.170
The seasoning is a bit plain, and 
the presentation is unacceptable,

08:36.170 --> 08:37.790
but I'm willing to compromise.

08:38.040 --> 08:40.360
The fish you cooked is pretty good, Lucas.

08:40.360 --> 08:41.640
Obviously!

08:42.770 --> 08:46.460
Hopefully you'll figure it 
out faster next time.

08:46.460 --> 08:49.530
You don't have to eat 
if you'd rather complain!

08:49.530 --> 08:52.550
I wouldn't want that. My apologies, Lucas.

08:53.780 --> 08:55.240
As long as you understand.

08:58.340 --> 09:00.600
Why did you have Lucas handle the cooking?

09:00.600 --> 09:03.470
It's more efficient if we split the labor.

09:03.470 --> 09:04.820
You manipulated him nicely.

09:25.220 --> 09:28.230
I'm amazed you can eat with that thing on.

09:29.160 --> 09:30.420
It is impressive, isn't it?

09:56.160 --> 10:01.340
I did some simple scouting around the
 island while gathering food yesterday.

10:11.300 --> 10:14.360
To start with, we're the only people here.

10:15.050 --> 10:19.180
I found the boats that 
you two washed up in,

10:19.640 --> 10:21.880
but they won't help us escape the island.

10:22.880 --> 10:27.950
There are two things we can do: wait for 
rescue, or find a way back ourselves.

10:28.480 --> 10:29.950
Is there any hope we'll be rescued?

10:29.950 --> 10:32.820
Jasmine is an AA-rank adventurer.

10:32.820 --> 10:35.840
I know she's alive, 
and that she'll find me.

10:36.210 --> 10:37.920
You really trust her, huh?

10:38.320 --> 10:39.990
Then what about leaving ourselves?

10:41.490 --> 10:43.700
We can't be that far from the mainland.

10:43.700 --> 10:45.520
We should be able to make it.

10:45.520 --> 10:46.920
Neither of those plans will work.

10:48.020 --> 10:51.000
Since we're stuck in this 
together, I'll enlighten you.

10:51.500 --> 10:53.810
This is the target of my quest.

10:53.810 --> 10:57.240
It can control weather, 
albeit on a limited scale.

10:57.240 --> 10:59.220
If we run into it out at sea,
we'll be done for.

11:00.330 --> 11:02.530
Then the fishing boats...

11:02.530 --> 11:04.480
And the boats we were all in...

11:04.480 --> 11:06.370
That was all thanks to this, most likely.

11:06.370 --> 11:09.100
Considering how dangerous 
this mana beast is,

11:09.100 --> 11:11.050
it makes sense that His Majesty the king

11:11.050 --> 11:13.360
would bring in the Wykes 
family to hunt it down.

11:13.360 --> 11:14.740
Do you have any more info on it?

11:15.200 --> 11:16.610
It tends to nest near water's edge,

11:16.610 --> 11:18.680
and claims the surrounding 
area as its territory.

11:19.120 --> 11:21.760
In other words, 
it's somewhere on this island.

11:21.760 --> 11:23.250
I'm going to burn it to cinders.

11:25.000 --> 11:26.250
Wait, Lucas.

11:27.890 --> 11:30.280
It'll be more effective 
if all three of us go.

11:31.370 --> 11:32.840
Just don't get in the way.

11:39.610 --> 11:40.750
Arthur...

11:46.660 --> 11:48.510
What are you doing here?

12:00.300 --> 12:02.870
Arthur's alive, isn't he?

12:04.600 --> 12:07.630
Thank goodness. Arthur...

12:10.540 --> 12:11.820
I'd better hurry.

12:17.290 --> 12:18.480
It's in there.

12:18.880 --> 12:19.850
Sure is.

12:19.850 --> 12:22.430
We can be sure that this is its nest.

12:22.820 --> 12:25.010
Can you start us off with 
something big, Lucas?

12:25.010 --> 12:26.170
Very well.

12:26.170 --> 12:28.690
I'll put on a display of 
the power we Wykes wield.

12:55.890 --> 12:58.090
How's that? Impressive?

12:58.300 --> 13:00.300
Yeah. Better than I expected.

13:00.300 --> 13:02.240
Maybe show a little restraint next time!

13:02.240 --> 13:07.020
I may have overdone it. 
Hopefully its mana core is intact.

13:08.640 --> 13:09.840
Is that...

13:09.840 --> 13:11.350
Get clear! Now!

13:28.520 --> 13:30.410
It's... kind of big.

13:30.410 --> 13:32.560
Yes. Just a bit.

13:39.900 --> 13:42.860
I'll keep it occupied. 
Whip up another big attack.

13:43.820 --> 13:46.640
I know! I was just about to do that!

13:46.860 --> 13:48.390
I can handle defense!

13:48.390 --> 13:49.570
Right.

13:49.570 --> 13:50.640
Let's go!

13:59.650 --> 14:02.510
Make a fool out of me, will you!

14:06.660 --> 14:07.910
Seriously?!

14:19.420 --> 14:21.300
What the hell is this thing?!

14:24.180 --> 14:26.860
We're not getting anywhere!

14:33.140 --> 14:34.190
<i>My attacks are effective,</i>

14:34.190 --> 14:37.770
<i>but almost instantly undone 
by its regenerative ability.</i>

14:37.770 --> 14:39.760
<i>I find the biodiversity...</i>

14:41.080 --> 14:44.180
<i>of the world I find myself in fascinating.</i>

14:45.400 --> 14:46.570
<i>It's worth a try.</i>

14:47.080 --> 14:48.450
Let's swap positions.

14:54.800 --> 14:56.330
Lucas, we need backup!

14:57.680 --> 14:59.270
I know!

15:02.930 --> 15:07.050
But who's gonna protect 
me if it turns this way?!

15:09.580 --> 15:11.300
Are you sure this is a good idea?!

15:11.300 --> 15:13.030
Yeah. Probably.

15:13.030 --> 15:14.060
Probably?!

15:14.440 --> 15:16.060
We don't have any other options.

15:16.760 --> 15:18.310
Fine!

15:20.290 --> 15:21.820
What's wrong, Lucas?

15:21.820 --> 15:25.190
I thought you were from the most powerful 
family of mages in the Sapin Kingdom!

15:25.880 --> 15:27.360
Do not mock me!

15:35.830 --> 15:38.580
I am Lucas Wykes!

15:49.620 --> 15:51.610
Stick to the plan, Elijah.

15:51.610 --> 15:52.720
Right!

15:58.720 --> 15:59.480
Elijah!

16:08.140 --> 16:09.990
It can't regenerate?

16:10.220 --> 16:11.740
Let's keep it up!

16:11.740 --> 16:13.120
Yeah!

16:33.730 --> 16:35.720
We beat it thanks to you, Elijah!

16:35.720 --> 16:38.520
All thanks to your plan, Note!

16:38.520 --> 16:42.650
And the Wykes family's renown 
is bound to grow yet again!

16:42.650 --> 16:44.400
There he goes again.

16:45.890 --> 16:47.440
<i>Those with great power</i>

16:47.440 --> 16:50.670
<i>must carry the responsibility 
and pressure that come with it.</i>

16:50.670 --> 16:54.600
<i>Maybe the concern I show for 
this young noble is because</i>

16:54.600 --> 16:58.020
<i>he reminds me of myself
 when I was younger.</i>

16:58.020 --> 16:58.930
What?

16:58.930 --> 16:59.910
Nothing.

17:00.250 --> 17:01.920
That was some impressive firepower.

17:02.220 --> 17:03.920
Of course!

17:09.440 --> 17:11.190
It's still alive.

17:12.530 --> 17:14.180
<i>I'm already exhausted.</i>

17:14.180 --> 17:16.140
<i>How much further can I push this?</i>

17:27.920 --> 17:30.200
There! Arthur!

17:37.170 --> 17:37.840
Dammit!

17:37.840 --> 17:39.950
Stay back! Stay away!

17:52.620 --> 17:53.680
Are you all right?!

17:53.680 --> 17:55.720
What about you, Jasmine? Are you okay?

18:05.920 --> 18:09.580
This is what an AA-rank adventurer can do?

18:09.580 --> 18:13.240
I-I am mildly impressed.

18:15.620 --> 18:18.980
I'm sorry. I should have known 
what we were getting into.

18:18.980 --> 18:21.210
I could say the same thing.

18:21.210 --> 18:22.330
But...

18:22.330 --> 18:26.010
We're a party, aren't we?

18:26.010 --> 18:27.100
Arthur...

18:27.880 --> 18:30.760
Thank you for coming to save me.

18:34.050 --> 18:36.760
Yeah. We're a party.

18:38.920 --> 18:40.310
Note!

18:40.770 --> 18:42.740
Don't let her get away!

18:42.740 --> 18:45.000
That mana core is mine!

18:45.000 --> 18:47.340
I forgot all about that!

19:02.260 --> 19:02.860
Wait.

19:02.860 --> 19:08.040
Whoa, hang on, you still 
haven't seen Arthur?

19:08.040 --> 19:12.040
I can't help it. We just seem 
to keep missing each other.

19:12.610 --> 19:14.050
I know what this is.

19:14.050 --> 19:16.050
Yeah, me too.

19:16.050 --> 19:18.180
Are you scared?

19:19.560 --> 19:21.810
Obviously not!

19:21.810 --> 19:26.290
Fine, then! I'll go right now! 
Just you watch!

19:26.290 --> 19:27.190
Tessia.

19:28.420 --> 19:29.190
What?

19:29.570 --> 19:31.440
Don't forget to pay for your share.

19:53.890 --> 19:54.960
<i>I can do this.</i>

19:55.650 --> 19:59.400
<i>I mean, I'm the princess 
of the Elenoir Kingdom.</i>

19:59.720 --> 20:02.470
<i>Visiting a friend I haven't 
seen in a while is nothing.</i>

20:03.360 --> 20:04.960
<i>Here we go, Tessia!</i>

20:12.140 --> 20:13.480
Can I help you with something?

20:16.140 --> 20:20.220
E-Excuse me!

20:21.130 --> 20:24.240
That girl was an elf.

20:26.420 --> 20:31.220
Looks like other races have 
started showing up in Xyrus!

20:31.220 --> 20:34.000
Guess that treaty is working out.

20:34.720 --> 20:36.510
That's welcome news to me!

20:54.010 --> 20:56.080
Things seem to be proceeding apace.

20:56.080 --> 20:59.480
Yes. They're performing admirably.

21:00.080 --> 21:03.020
But it's still not enough.

21:09.130 --> 21:13.000
I'll need to find one that's 
even more powerful...

21:16.650 --> 21:19.260
for the appointed day.
